{"id": "EUVD-2026-108689", "enisaUuid": "e92d6669-2ec6-3067-b7cd-c0e6b47ea980", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet/mlx5: HWS, Handle destroying table that has a miss table\n\nIf a table has a miss table that was created by\n'mlx5hws_table_set_default_miss' API function, its miss_tbl\nkeeps the table that points to it in a list.\nIf such table is deleted, we need to also remove it from the\nmiss_tbl list, otherwise the node in miss_tbl list will contain\ngarbage.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16b81428f7b5f253ab30a998bc4f4ecd1c8823f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6efdc212627cecf33b594256ae4460b4c52a126a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/60e9e82f162ab7399373ff2185119289e4f6dc06"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98895"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "14ba146a-5cca-30ec-841f-b1fb0c4fdd0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "2b533a9b-1010-3126-90a1-46863ff41a4c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "62858ab4-8123-3cc0-be63-89e691da3a2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <16b81428f7b5f253ab30a998bc4f4ecd1c8823f8"}, {"id": "a8f7157a-d325-3aa2-8731-1f19e6c843a8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "ac159b72-8123-31ac-b5ce-97231b7b0969", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "d184d8f9-a5b1-3e68-9b06-b31ddd3c4eb6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <6efdc212627cecf33b594256ae4460b4c52a126a"}, {"id": "d68dbaf6-ed33-3991-b078-3a0aeac0644c", "product":